u$ be a nonzero nonnegative Radon measure, $f$ an $\R^m$-valued Radon measure, $ eta$ a symmetric matrix-valued Radon measure, and $\mathfrak m$ a signed Radon measure on $\Omega$. Suppose that  egin{equation}  egin{pmatrix}
u&f^{m t}\ f& eta\end{pmatrix} \quad\hbox{is a positive semidefinite matrix-valued measure}, \qquad d_0=	r eta, \end{equation} and that, in distributions,  egin{equation} 
