u=2f,\qquad \diver f=d_0,\qquad \int\diver X\,\dd\mathfrak m =\int DX:\dd eta \quad(X\in C_c^\infty(\Omega;\R^m)). \end{equation} Assume also that for every open $\Omega'\Subset\Omega$ there is a constant $C_{\Omega'}$ such that, on $\Omega'$,  egin{equation} 2\mathfrak m\le d_0,\qquad |\mathfrak m|\le C_{\Omega'}d_0. \end{equation} Let $Z\subset\Omega$ be a Borel set such that for each $x\in Z$,  egin{equation} 2l^2\int\phi_{x,l}\,\dd\mathfrak m \ge\int\psi_{x,l}\,\dd
u \end{equation} for every sufficiently small $l>0$. Then $\dim_{\Hh}Z\le m-1$.
